S-CI-1 — Did CI ever actually run?
Date: 2026-07-30
Method: gh CLI + GitHub REST API against the live repo (bsidenberg/fpb-marketing-bot).
Read-only throughout.

Commands run and raw output:

$ gh auth status
  Logged in to github.com account bsidenberg, token scopes: gist, read:org, repo

$ gh run list --repo bsidenberg/fpb-marketing-bot --limit 30 --json databaseId,status,conclusion,createdAt,headBranch,name
  []
  (exit 0 — the call succeeded; the array is genuinely empty, not an auth failure)

$ gh workflow list --repo bsidenberg/fpb-marketing-bot --all
  (empty — no workflows registered, active or disabled)

$ gh api repos/bsidenberg/fpb-marketing-bot/actions/workflows --jq '.total_count'
  0

$ gh api repos/bsidenberg/fpb-marketing-bot --jq '{full_name, created_at, pushed_at, default_branch}'
  {"full_name":"bsidenberg/fpb-marketing-bot","created_at":"2026-03-24T23:05:22Z",
   "pushed_at":"2026-07-07T20:19:46Z","default_branch":"main"}

$ git log --all --oneline -- .github/
  (empty — .github/ has never been committed to ANY local branch, ever)

$ git ls-remote --heads origin
  92567dd5450b77e3a0b21dafee52233817df4b7e  refs/heads/fix/production-triage
  8df0789b6fee523b5f1a4cfdf392eabbedffa3f4  refs/heads/main
  4e8bb1cd75c3eda6a71a4c210d0448b5f0a0255c  refs/heads/v0/bsidenberg-114604b1

=== Finding ===

**GitHub Actions CI has NEVER run in this repository, not once, on any
branch, in its entire history.** Zero registered workflows (API
total_count: 0), zero runs (gh run list: empty array, not an error), and
`.github/workflows/verify.yml` has never been committed to git at all
locally (git log --all shows nothing for that path) — so it was never in
a position to be pushed and picked up by GitHub Actions in the first
place. The repo's last push to GitHub was 2026-07-07, and the workflow
file's own timestamp (2026-07-12 04:01, per the prime-audit.zip listing
inspected under S-CLEAN-1) postdates that push — it was authored locally
after the last time anything reached GitHub.

=== This corrects the framing in HARNESS.md §4.1, SDR-1 instance 1 ===

The table there reads: "`.github/workflows/verify.yml` ran `npm run lint
--if-present` with no `lint` script defined... CI green. Evidence logs
attested 'ALL CHECKS PASSED (2/2)'... Months, until 2026-07-28."

That conflates two DIFFERENT gates:
  (a) the LOCAL `scripts/verify.ps1` gate, run by agents/CI-equivalent
      sessions and producing the evidence logs cited (e.g.
      S-08A-verify-2026-07-13_1727.log) — this DID run, repeatedly, and DID
      silently skip lint via the same `--if-present`-shaped guard
      (`if ($scripts.ContainsKey("lint"))`). That half of the claim is true
      and already evidenced.
  (b) GitHub Actions CI (`.github/workflows/verify.yml`) — this is the
      "CI" the sentence's grammatical subject names, and per this
      session's investigation, it has NEVER run. Not "ran green while
      skipping lint" — never invoked at all, because it was never
      committed, so GitHub never had it to run.

**"CI green" is not a true historical claim.** There was no CI to be green
or red. The "months" duration and the fixed defect (silent lint-skip) are
both real for the LOCAL gate; attributing them to GitHub Actions CI
specifically is incorrect and is corrected here per SDR-2 (a claim in the
harness's own document is a hypothesis until the repo confirms it,
including when the harness itself asserts it).

**Consequence:** now that `.github/workflows/verify.yml` is committed
(this session's earlier housekeeping commit under S-LINT-1 staged it,
though nothing has actually been committed tonight — see the git-commit-
blocked finding), the FIRST time GitHub Actions will ever run for this
repo is whenever Brian pushes. There is no prior CI history to compare
against; the "3/3" vs "2/2" gate distinction documented in HARNESS.md
describes the LOCAL verify.ps1 gate's evolution, not GitHub Actions',
which starts from zero runs regardless.
